  "findings": [
    "Both arms offered 60 journeys/s for 300 seconds; 18,000 scheduled, dispatched and confirmed each. Zero customer errors, generator drops or client retries. Each reconciled 18,000 durable payments, bookings and tickets, zero duplicate booked seats, and complete global/Kafka queue drain and restoration.",
    "Claim mean fell from 9.2467 to 8.6418 ms (6.54%); due-to-claim mean fell from 56.8714 to 49.9914 ms (12.10%); hold-to-ticket worst-shard p95 fell from 1,835.59 to 1,667.60 ms (9.15%).",
    "Primary offered-window CPU was 70.7070% versus 70.6076%, a reduction of only 0.0994 percentage points. No material CPU reduction or higher-capacity measurement. Payment HTTP p95 increased 4.90%; simulator delivery mean rose from 43.6582 to 51.6573 ms (18.32%), and its histogram p95 bucket rose from 100 to 250 ms. The benefit is mixed.",
    "Observer-lifetime callback backlog peak fell from 41 to 27, but p95 queue length rose from 9 to 12. API acquisition-failure counters were zero in both arms; slow API phase records fell from 81 to 27. Recovered consumer 55P03 batches were 6 versus 0, and recovered simulator delivery-error calls were 25 versus 20. Zero customer errors does not mean zero internal transient failures.",
    "Primary consumer CPU averaged 0.5816 versus 0.5893 cores over observer lifetimes, the largest movable background role. These role means and phase metrics include observer and completion tails. Nested timings cannot be added, and their windows differ from offered-window CPU.",
    "One sequential matched five-minute pair supports no statistical significance, 84 tickets/s, 300,000 tickets/hour, flash-opening or 18,000-seat projection qualification. The historical unresolved fixture evidence remains unchanged."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Retain the safe atomic-claim candidate as a qualified optimization, without claiming new capacity or changing the restored normal deployment. Next integrate a fixed-budget background-service placement profile for the existing secondary ECS, with measured role CPU guiding the split. Locally qualify it before load, then qualify 84 paid-and-issued tickets/s. Use existing machines and sizes."
